By morning, the little kitten was gone.

Barnaby sat by the empty basket, watching the moon through the window. He had gone on an adventure, faced the unknown, and returned with a friend—but the friend had not stayed. He was no longer just a house cat. He was Barnaby the Brave, the rescuer of the Old Oak, and he carried a sadness that no sunbeam could warm.
